[Google Antigravity](https://antigravity.google) is Google's agentic development platform. Its IDE includes an **Agent Manager**, where AI agents work through coding tasks with an understanding of your codebase, and an MCP Store for connecting agents to external tools.

# How does the integration work?

The [Appwrite MCP server](/docs/tooling/ai/mcp-servers) connects Antigravity's agents to your Appwrite project through the [Model Context Protocol](https://modelcontextprotocol.io). It is a hosted server at `https://mcp.appwrite.io/` that uses the HTTP transport and signs you in with OAuth, so there is nothing to install and no API key to create.

Once connected, an agent can look up your projects, read and change resources such as users, databases, and tables, and search the Appwrite documentation while it codes. Changes go through a separate write tool that requires confirmation, and each change carries a short reason that appears in your project's **Activity** tab.

{% info title="Self-hosted Appwrite" %}
The hosted MCP server authenticates against Appwrite Cloud. If you self-host Appwrite, use the [local MCP server](/docs/advanced/self-hosting/mcp) instead. It runs on your machine over stdio and connects to your instance with an API key.
{% /info %}

# How to implement

To connect Google Antigravity to Appwrite, there are several steps you must complete:

## Step 1: Set up your Appwrite project

First, [create an account on Appwrite Cloud](/sign-up) if you haven't already, and create a project. You don't need an API key: Antigravity opens your browser so you can sign in to Appwrite when it first connects.

## Step 2: Add the Appwrite MCP server to Antigravity

In the Agent window, open the **...** menu and go to **Manage MCP Servers** in the MCP Store. Click **View raw config** and add the Appwrite server to `mcp_config.json`:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "appwrite": {
      "serverUrl": "https://mcp.appwrite.io/"
    }
  }
}
```

Antigravity needs the `serverUrl` key for remote MCP servers. Using `url` or `httpUrl` instead makes tool registration fail without an error.

Sign in to your Appwrite account in the browser window that opens and authorize access, then return to **Manage MCP Servers** and click refresh.

## Step 3: Test the integration

Open the **Agent Manager** and try prompts like:

- `Create a new user in my Appwrite project`
- `List all databases in my project`
- `Show me the tables in my database`
- `How do I set up real-time subscriptions in Appwrite?`

